{"id":"e15691d5-28b7-437f-a3c4-409865c03db1","object":"chat.completion","created":1795243784,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"WITH first_orders AS (\n  SELECT c.customer_unique_id,\n         DATE_TRUNC('month', MIN(o.order_purchase_timestamp)) AS first_order_month\n  FROM orders o\n  JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\n  WHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled', 'unavailable')\n    AND c.customer_unique_id IS NOT NULL\n    AND o.order_purchase_timestamp IS NOT NULL\n  GROUP BY c.customer_unique_id\n),\nmonthly AS (\n  SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS month,\n         CASE\n           WHEN DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) = fo.first_order_month THEN 'NEW'\n           WHEN DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) > fo.first_order_month THEN 'RETURNING'\n           ELSE NULL\n         END AS cohort,\n         SUM(oi.price + oi.freight_value) AS gmv\n  FROM orders o\n  JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\n  JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n  LEFT JOIN first_orders fo ON fo.customer_unique_id = c.customer_unique_id\n  WHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled', 'unavailable')\n    AND o.order_purchase_timestamp >= '2018-01-01'\n    AND o.order_purchase_timestamp < '2019-01-01'\n  GROUP BY 1, 2\n)\nSELECT m.month::date AS month,\n       ROUND(SUM(monthly.gmv) FILTER (WHERE monthly.cohort = 'NEW'), 2) AS new_customer_gmv,\n       ROUND(SUM(monthly.gmv) FILTER (WHERE monthly.cohort = 'RETURNING'), 2) AS returning_customer_gmv\nFROM generate_series('2018-01-01'::timestamp, '2018-12-01'::timestamp, INTERVAL '1 month') AS m(month)\nLEFT JOIN monthly ON monthly.month = m.month\nGROUP BY m.month\nORDER BY m.month\nLIMIT 12;","reasoning_content":"We need answer SQL only. Need craft. Need parse Chinese.\n\nQuestion: \"2018年逐自然月输出有效订单含运费GMV两位，按自然人全部历史首次有效下单月区分新老客；输出月份、新客GMV、老客GMV全部12个月，缺金额事实为NULL。\"\n\nNeed 2018 monthly, output months, new customer GMV, returning customer GMV, all 12 months, missing amount facts NULL. GMV with freight two decimals. Valid orders excludes canceled/unavailable. Cohort dynamic first effective order month over all history. Need classify each order in 2018 by natural person's first valid order month: NEW if same month as first, RETURNING if later. What about NULL? User asks new and old only. Need output month, new GMV, old GMV all 12 months. Missing amount facts NULL. Need ensure months Jan-Dec 2018 even if no facts. Need all 12 months. Use calendar generate_series. Left join monthly aggregates.\n\nNeed follow metric customer_cohort recommended structure. We need calculate per month new gmv, returning gmv. Need handle unknown identities? They ask new/old. Maybe exclude NULL categories? Let's reason. Output months, new GMV, old GMV. GMV for valid orders. For new/old classification. Need all history first order in valid orders. Use first_orders CTE from all valid orders with customer_unique_id and purchase timestamp. Then classify 2018 orders. For each order, join orders to customers, first_orders. Need group by month and cohort. Aggregate order_items price+freight. Need avoid amount amplification? order_items is one row per item, order can have multiple items. Summing oi.price+freight across order_items is correct fact grain. Need not count orders. GMV sum per item. Need join orders to order_items. If classify orders and sum order_items. Need not overcount due to customer duplicates? orders.customer_id unique customer record, each order one customer_id. first_orders by customer_unique_id. Good.\n\nNeed months all 12. We can generate series '2018-01-01' to '2018-12-01' month. For each month, left join aggregate by month with new/returning. Need output month maybe DATE_TRUNC month or TO_CHAR? User says output month. Could output month as date (date_trunc). Need \"逐自然月\" maybe month column. Could output DATE_TRUNC('month', ...)::date AS month. Need all 12 months. Missing amount facts NULL. For months no GMV, null. If there are facts but no new/old? Should be NULL. Use SUM with FILTER? Could aggregate in CTE.\n\nNeed valid orders. first_orders CTE:\nWITH first_orders AS (\n SELECT c.customer_unique_id, DATE_TRUNC('month', MIN(o.order_purchase_timestamp)) AS first_order_month\n FROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id=o.customer_id\n WHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled','unavailable')\n AND c.customer_unique_id IS NOT NULL\n AND o.order_purchase_timestamp IS NOT NULL\n GROUP BY c.customer_unique_id\n),\nmonthly AS (\n SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) AS month,\n   CASE WHEN DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) = fo.first_order_month THEN 'new'\n        WHEN DATE_TRUNC('month', o.order_purchase_timestamp) > fo.first_order_month THEN 'returning'\n        ELSE NULL END AS cohort,\n   SUM(oi.price + oi.freight_value) AS gmv\n FROM orders o\n JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id=o.customer_id\n JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id=o.order_id\n LEFT JOIN first_orders fo ON fo.customer_unique_id=c.customer_unique_id\n WHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled','unavailable')\n   AND o.order_purchase_timestamp >= '2018-01-01' AND o.order_purchase_timestamp < '2019-01-01'\n GROUP BY 1,2\n)\nSELECT months.month::date AS month,\n  ROUND(SUM(monthly.gmv) FILTER (WHERE monthly.cohort='new')::numeric,2) AS new_customer_gmv,\n...\nFROM generate_series('2018-01-01'::timestamp, '2018-12-01'::timestamp, '1 month') AS months(month)\nLEFT JOIN monthly ON monthly.month = months.month\nGROUP BY months.month\nORDER BY months.month;\n\nNeed be careful ROUND type. monthly.gmv is numeric because price/freight numeric. SUM numeric. FILTER returns numeric. ROUND numeric,2 okay. But if no rows, SUM filter null and round null. Good. Need use alias. But grouping by months.month. Could instead use conditional aggregation in single query. Need all months. Use generate_series. Need avoid group by month with monthly.gmv rows multiple cohorts (two per month). We can aggregate. Use SUM(monthly.gmv) FILTER.\n\nAlternative pivot:\nSELECT m.month::date AS month,\n ROUND(SUM(g.gmv) FILTER (WHERE g.cohort='NEW'), 2) AS new_customer_gmv,\n ROUND(SUM(g.gmv) FILTER (WHERE g.cohort='RETURNING'), 2) AS returning_customer_gmv\n...\nNeed names maybe new_gmv, returning_gmv. Good.\n\nPotential issue: first_orders includes all historical valid orders. For 2018 orders, we use first_order_month. If first order month after 2018? impossible for 2018 order. If first order month before 2018 -> returning. If same month -> new. Good.\n\nWhat about orders with missing customer_unique_id? Then first_orders null; cohort null. GMV excluded from new/old. User only asks new/old. Fine. But does \"按自然人全部历史首次有效下单月区分新老客\" require only known natural persons. Yes. Unknown not classified. We can keep unknown not output. Good.\n\nNeed \"有效订单含运费GMV两位\": sum price+freight. Use oi.price + oi.freight_value. Valid order excludes canceled/unavailable. Good.\n\nNeed all 12 months even no GMV. Use generate_series. Need month column maybe date. For all months with missing amount facts null. If month has orders but no new/old? unknown could be ignored. But if month has only unknown, new/old null. Fine.\n\nNeed maybe include only months in 2018. Good.\n\nNeed avoid using \"customer_cohort\" metric exactly? We have same logic. The metric says output constraint \"按用户要求输出周期和所需指标\". Good.\n\nNeed maybe use first_orders CTE as recommended. Need not use user_tags. Good.\n\nNeed consider order items join: Some valid orders may have no order_items? Then GMV missing. If no order_items, no amount facts, should NULL. Our aggregate ignores. For month with only valid orders no items, no row -> null. Good. But if some orders no items and others have, sum existing. Good.\n\nNeed ensure all 12 months. generate_series with timestamp. Use '2018-01-01'::timestamp and '2018-12-01'::timestamp interval '1 month'. That returns 12. Good.\n\nNeed SQL only no code fences. Need